WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.890
- Happy belated birthday, a few weeks ago

00:00:01.890 --> 00:00:03.210
you had a huge birthday.

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:04.043
It's a big birthday.

00:00:04.043 --> 00:00:06.090
- You know Kelly, I
don't count them anymore.

00:00:06.090 --> 00:00:06.923
- You don't?

00:00:06.923 --> 00:00:09.270
- No, I mean, I feel blessed
to have another day of life

00:00:09.270 --> 00:00:10.103
for sure, but-

00:00:10.103 --> 00:00:11.550
- That's why I do count them.

00:00:11.550 --> 00:00:12.383
Not everybody gets them.

00:00:12.383 --> 00:00:13.230
- We're not gonna talk numbers.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:14.100
- Oh, no you don't have to.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:17.100
But not everybody gets
you know, that many years.

00:00:17.100 --> 00:00:18.540
So it is a blessing.

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.373
- It is true.

00:00:19.373 --> 00:00:20.206
- Yeah, and it's good to celebrate.

00:00:20.206 --> 00:00:22.560
I'm opposite, I don't care about age.

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:23.393
I don't really care.

00:00:23.393 --> 00:00:24.510
- Age is a funny thing.

00:00:24.510 --> 00:00:27.140
You know, what I find is that, my God

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:30.900
as I've gotten older, I
just get more sensitive.

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:32.190
Like-
- Oh yeah.

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:35.460
- I'll watch watch your
show, your other show.

00:00:35.460 --> 00:00:39.720
I'll watch you on "The Voice"
and I'll watch a young singer

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.060
who aspires to be a
superstar like you and-

00:00:42.060 --> 00:00:42.960
- [Kelly] Oh, the stories get you?

00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:44.850
- And the stories, for sure, yeah,

00:00:44.850 --> 00:00:46.890
but the song itself will move me to tears.

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:49.350
And my son who's 17 and kind of tough,

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:50.989
looks over at me and goes-

00:00:50.989 --> 00:00:52.004
- [Kelly] What are you doing?

00:00:52.004 --> 00:00:53.610
- Why are you crying?

00:00:53.610 --> 00:00:54.612
Like, why are you crying?

00:00:54.612 --> 00:00:56.880
I said, buddy, "I cry
at coffee commercials".

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:58.140
Like, I don't know why I'm crying.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:59.730
- Yeah.
- As I've gotten older,

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:00.990
I don't know what's going on with me.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:01.823
But I don't know, maybe it's-

00:01:01.823 --> 00:01:02.656
- [Kelly] That's a man thing, I feel like-

00:01:02.656 --> 00:01:04.571
- Facing mortality now,
I don't know what it is.

00:01:04.571 --> 00:01:05.404
- I don't know.

00:01:05.404 --> 00:01:06.803
But I also feel like, men I think you've-

00:01:06.803 --> 00:01:09.420
I think you've, especially my generation,

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:10.680
your generation like, they were taught

00:01:10.680 --> 00:01:12.510
they weren't allowed to be emotional.

00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:14.700
You were supposed to be strong
or whatever, like growing up.

00:01:14.700 --> 00:01:16.530
And I feel like, I don't know
over the course of the time,

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:17.497
I think you should go
on, you're just like,

00:01:17.497 --> 00:01:18.870
"Whatever, it's touching.

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:19.830
I'm gonna let it out.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:20.817
I'm gonna cry."

00:01:20.817 --> 00:01:21.650
- That's not the-

00:01:21.650 --> 00:01:24.319
Yeah, that's not the lesson
I teach in my household.

00:01:24.319 --> 00:01:25.152
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:25.152 --> 00:01:26.443
You're free and welcome
to cry at any moment.

00:01:26.443 --> 00:01:27.750
- [Kelly] I know, but we're in different-

00:01:27.750 --> 00:01:29.015
I'm teaching my children
differently as well,

00:01:29.015 --> 00:01:30.600
but I just meant from our generation

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:31.433
it was always like, I'm from the South.

00:01:31.433 --> 00:01:33.077
Like, it was like, don't show emotion.

00:01:33.077 --> 00:01:33.910
- Oh, of course.
- That is weak.

00:01:33.910 --> 00:01:35.853
- Yeah, yeah, yeah.
- Whatever.

